WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.080
The hawkfish is a brightly colored, orange-spotted&nbsp;
coral reef dwelling fish with an incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.280
reproductive talent. Hawkfish may begin their&nbsp;
lives as females, but when there are too many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.400
female hawkfish in their habitat, they have&nbsp;
the ability to turn into males of the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.920
species. This allows the new male hawkfish&nbsp;
to take on some of the reproductive burden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:28.080
allowing the females more mating options. Not&nbsp;
only can the hawkfish change its sex, it can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.840
also change it back! A hawkfish that has turned&nbsp;
male can revert back to female if the population&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:40.080
makeup changes, and more females are needed.
This incredible talent is not limited to hawkfish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:46.480
either, gender bending is prevalent throughout the&nbsp;
animal kingdom. Frogs, bearded dragons, clownfish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.760
and many other animals have the ability to&nbsp;
change sex if the situation calls for it.&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.560
You might be sitting at home wondering, what’s&nbsp;
with all the animal talk? I came here for an SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:02.080
video, not a biology lesson. Well just trust us,&nbsp;
we’re getting there. While it’s simple for many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.360
other animals, human beings have a great deal&nbsp;
more difficulty changing their sex and gender&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.720
characteristics. It can require surgery and years&nbsp;
of hormone replacement therapy to get the kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:20.800
results a clownfish gets overnight. Unless, of&nbsp;
course, a human gets their hands on SCP-113.&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.280
SCP-113 is a small, polished red stone resembling&nbsp;
a piece of jasper. When studied closely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:32.880
in spite of its resemblance, it was found to&nbsp;
not be jasper or any other identifiable type&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.440
of rock. When placed against the flesh&nbsp;
of a living thing with sex chromosomes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:43.280
the organisms gender and sex-associated physical&nbsp;
characteristics are changed in some way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.800
These effects were first tested on humans with&nbsp;
an unnamed D-class. The D-Class was placed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.440
a sterile examination room and hooked up to&nbsp;
a variety of sensors and equipment designed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:59.680
to monitor their biological state, health, and&nbsp;
any changes to their body that might take place.&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.720
First, the D-class was instructed to open their&nbsp;
hand, and close the stone in their fist. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:11.520
contact between their skin and SCP-113 kickstarted&nbsp;
the first stage of the transformation process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:17.440
Stage one lasted approximately 0.2 seconds, as&nbsp;
the stone bonded with the cells it was touching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.160
causing a chemical change and leaving a small&nbsp;
amount of tissue damage comparable to a mild&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.080
burn. As soon as this process began, the D-Class&nbsp;
could not remove the stone from their hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.560
Unsettled, they attempted to shake the stone&nbsp;
loose from their skin, but to no avail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.160
It was firmly attached to the skin, and would&nbsp;
not be removed until the process was complete.&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.440
The second stage of transformation followed,&nbsp;
lasting approximately 20 seconds. The D-class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.000
reported feeling nauseous, and promptly&nbsp;
vomited onto the floor of the exam room. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.240
they reported a stinging sensation throughout&nbsp;
their body, like being pricked with tiny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.360
needles all over. These sensations have been&nbsp;
attributed to a low-level electromagnetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:03.680
wave released by SCP-113 during this phase,&nbsp;
which was picked up by one of the monitors.&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:09.680
After the nausea passed, the scientists observing&nbsp;
the D-Class’s monitors began taking furious notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.480
shocked at what was occurring. Though the&nbsp;
modality of it was unclear, the subject’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.560
cellular makeup was beginning to change. Some&nbsp;
of their cells were registering as nonhuman, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.400
others were registering as human stem cells. At&nbsp;
this point, the D-class began to scream in agony.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.840
All of the sensory nerves in their body were&nbsp;
stimulated at once, and their brain activity was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.120
overwhelming, at a level similar to a seizure.
Finally, once the screaming stopped and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:43.360
D-class had gone still, the rock came loose from&nbsp;
their hand and clattered to the floor. After this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:48.560
a full physical was performed, and the D-Class&nbsp;
was determined to have undergone dramatic physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.160
changes, all of their primary and secondary&nbsp;
sexual characteristics altered permanently.&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.920
While SCP-113’s effect on humans with binary&nbsp;
gender identities - male and female - have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.160
studied, it is still difficult to determine&nbsp;
the sort of impact that the stone might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:10.160
on someone with a nonbinary gender identity, or&nbsp;
if the stone in fact takes gender identity into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:16.240
account at all. There is some evidence that the&nbsp;
stone is impacted by gender identity, though this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:23.040
is not always consistent. While SCP-113 alters&nbsp;
the physiology of the test subject, it has no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.640
impact on the mind. The subject’s gender identity&nbsp;
remains the same before and after any testing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.920
with the stone. In the case of one intersex&nbsp;
individual who was exposed to the stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.960
their secondary and primary sex characteristics&nbsp;
changed to those that would be more affirming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.320
to the individual’s gender identity.
However, as this is still very inconsistent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.600
unpredictable, not to mention possibly accompanied&nbsp;
by side effects that have not been determined yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:56.000
SCP-113 should not be considered a safe or&nbsp;
viable alternative to gender confirmation surgery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.840
for transgender individuals who might be seeking&nbsp;
it. Further research is required on the subject.&nbsp;

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:07.280
Ordinarily it is standard scientific practice&nbsp;
to test on animals before testing on humans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.720
However, the SCP Foundation isn’t exactly&nbsp;
known for its standard research practices.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.280
After sufficient human trials had been&nbsp;
conducted, the Foundation researchers studying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:23.680
SCP-113 decided to test its effects on other,&nbsp;
nonhuman organisms. There was a great deal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:29.200
curiosity about how it might impact various&nbsp;
animals, especially those whose sexual dimorphism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:35.600
or indeed entire relationship to sex and gender&nbsp;
is fundamentally different from that of humans.&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:41.360
With standard cats, rats, and dogs, the impact&nbsp;
was essentially the same as that on humans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.120
First, the stone binds to the skin. Then, it&nbsp;
emits an electromagnetic wave causing some nausea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:52.000
and vomiting. Next, the sensory nerves are&nbsp;
stimulated for 20 seconds as the cells become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:57.520
altered. Finally, the stone falls away from the&nbsp;
skin and the transformation has been completed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:02.960
Interesting at first, but after the 20th rat&nbsp;
it starts to become a little mundane. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:09.680
exposure of certain other species to&nbsp;
SCP-113 resulted in some unusual effects.&nbsp;

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:16.720
When a number of Komodo dragons were exposed to&nbsp;
SCP-113, their chromosomes changed from ZW/ZZ&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:23.120
to WW, resulting in the eventual deaths of the&nbsp;
reptiles. When nematodes, which are either male&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:29.280
or hermaphroditic, were exposed, no males were&nbsp;
produced during the experiment. Male nematodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.680
changed and became hermaphroditic, and the&nbsp;
hermaphroditic specimens were completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:39.040
unaffected as far as the researchers could tell.&nbsp;
Earthworms that were exposed to the stone were not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:45.280
transformed at all, and the transformation process&nbsp;
stopped during stage two every single time.&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.440
Several of the previously mentioned&nbsp;
animals were used as test subjects as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.240
in order to determine what effect the stone would&nbsp;
have on a creature that already naturally changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:59.200
its sex characteristics. Clownfish exposed&nbsp;
to the stone experienced no change to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:05.200
sex characteristics, but bizarrely did change&nbsp;
color from white and orange to a vivid blue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:10.320
No adverse effects were identified.
Bearded dragons exposed to SCP-113&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.320
spontaneously began to lay eggs, which&nbsp;
were immediately retrieved and placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:19.040
into incubators for observation. Once&nbsp;
hatched, the eggs contained ordinary baby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:24.400
bearded dragons that seemed to have no altered&nbsp;
physiology or residual effects from the stone.&nbsp;

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:29.040
The hawkfish exposed to the stone simply&nbsp;
transformed the same way they would in the wild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.080
from female to male, just at a faster rate&nbsp;
than they would under natural circumstances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.720
The rest of the animals tested had the same&nbsp;
result as the earthworm. The stone simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:44.080
disengaged from the test subject during stage two&nbsp;
of the transformation, as if it was giving up.&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.520
As SCP-113 is classified as safe, and only&nbsp;
impacts those who deliberately come into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.560
physical contact with it, its containment&nbsp;
procedures are relatively simple. The stone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.560 --> 00:08:00.800
is kept in standard storage at Site 23, and may be&nbsp;
handled with laboratory gloves. No living being is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:08.720
permitted to be exposed to SCP-113 unless it has&nbsp;
been officially approved. If exposed to SCP-113,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:14.640
personnel must be kept under medical observation&nbsp;
for 7 days in order to study its impact, and make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:20.880
sure no unexpected adverse effects are present.
After conducting a variety of animal trials, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:27.680
research time assigned to SCP-113 became curious&nbsp;
yet again about its impact on human test subjects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:34.960
Not on new subjects, but those that had already&nbsp;
been transformed by SCP-113 in one way or another.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.600
They wanted to determine what would happen&nbsp;
to someone who was re-exposed to the stone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:43.920
Would it reverse its own effects, essentially&nbsp;
turning them back to the person they were before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:50.160
the experiment? Would it transform them further?&nbsp;
Would it harm them? In an attempt to find out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:55.200
several of the original D-class personnel used in&nbsp;
113’s human trials were brought back for another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:01.120
round of experimentation, as well as a new D-class&nbsp;
to test the effects of immediate re-exposure.&nbsp;

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.520
First, the D-Class who had never been&nbsp;
exposed to SCP-113 had the stone placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.880
on his bare arm. Immediately, it attached&nbsp;
itself to him and the transformation began.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:15.440
After the transformation was complete, and&nbsp;
the rock detached from his arm, the attending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:21.440
scientists waited a duration of 60 seconds before&nbsp;
reattaching it. In order to avoid excessive tissue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:27.600
damage, the stone was placed on his other arm for&nbsp;
the second trial. Almost immediately, the subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:33.040
began to cry out in intense pain, writhing on&nbsp;
the exam table and begging for the stone to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.480
removed. Of course, at this point it had already&nbsp;
bound to his cells and could not be taken off.&nbsp;

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:44.880
During stage two his liver began to swell and he&nbsp;
began to enter the early phases of kidney failure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.720
By the time stage four was complete&nbsp;
and the stone could be removed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.440
the subject had passed out from the pain. An&nbsp;
immediate physical examination determined that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:59.120
the subject had significant damage to his liver&nbsp;
and kidneys, as well as loss of bone density and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:04.720
massive tissue damage on the arm where the stone&nbsp;
had been placed. Finally, his genitals appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:10.080
to have completely disappeared, leaving a&nbsp;
smooth surface behind on the pubic area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:16.400
like that of a doll. The subject died a few hours&nbsp;
later from organ failure and internal bleeding.&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.120
The rest of the D-classes were understandably&nbsp;
reluctant to be re-exposed to the stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:26.560
but unfortunately for them and luckily for the&nbsp;
Foundation, they didn’t have much of a choice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.320
Security locked the door to the examination&nbsp;
room, and the experimentation proceeded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.200
as planned. Re-exposure after a significant&nbsp;
amount of time had passed had a much higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.840
success rate than immediate re-exposure, and&nbsp;
the rest of the test subjects survived their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:48.320
second transformation at the hands of SCP-113.
However, it did not return them to the state they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:53.840
were in before their first exposure to the stone.&nbsp;
Some of them experienced no physical changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:58.480
at all, save for a small amount of tissue&nbsp;
damage where the stone touched their skin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:03.440
Others experienced physical changes that had&nbsp;
nothing to do with their sex characteristics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:08.640
One subject’s eyes changed color from green to&nbsp;
purple, while another subject suffering from male&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:14.000
pattern baldness emerged from the experiment with&nbsp;
a full head of hair. Some of the changes were more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.800
dramatic. One subject ended up with feathers&nbsp;
sprouting all over the surface of her skin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:23.520
Another lost all of his teeth.
One particularly odd test subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:29.920
seemed completely ordinary and unchanged, until&nbsp;
his physical examination. During the exam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:35.120
it was discovered that all of his internal&nbsp;
organs had changed places inside of his body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:40.560
their configuration turned completely upside&nbsp;
down. He seemed otherwise unharmed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:45.120
able to function as normal, and still&nbsp;
works at the Foundation to this day.&nbsp;

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:51.440
Even when exposure is spaced out, the more&nbsp;
times a person comes into contact with SCP-113,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:57.040
the stranger the effects get. The details have&nbsp;
been expunged from the official Foundation file,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:03.760
but there are rumors that one test subject, after&nbsp;
their fifth exposure to SCP-113, transformed into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:10.640
something completely inhuman and possibly deadly.
Like I said, the details have been removed from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:17.520
the file, but word gets around. Especially&nbsp;
words like “claws” and “acid tentacles.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:23.600
Those could just be rumors, but who knows?&nbsp;
Biology is full of mysteries, and there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.400
still so much we do not understand about the&nbsp;
natural world and the ways in which living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:35.120
things can transform for better or for much worse.
Perhaps some mysteries, especially the mystery of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:41.600
SCP-113, are better left alone.
Now go check out “SCP-004 - 12&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:48.000
Rusty Keys and the Door” and “SCP-500 -&nbsp;
Panacea” for more unusual object SCP’s!

